From: Arnaldo Carvalho de Melo <acme@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Jan 2026 01:15:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] perf jitdump: Constify variables storing the result of
 strchr() on const tables
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.40
Git-commit: 68abacb0686651dd3f0bbce2fa94b438afeb2fc4

commit 68abacb0686651dd3f0bbce2fa94b438afeb2fc4 upstream.

As newer glibcs will propagate the const attribute of the searched table
to its return.

Signed-off-by: Arnaldo Carvalho de Melo <acme@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 tools/perf/util/jitdump.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c b/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c
index b062b1f234b6..28d32e3cfdba 100644
--- a/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c
+++ b/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c
@@ -754,7 +754,7 @@ jit_inject(struct jit_buf_desc *jd, const char *path)
 static int
 jit_detect(const char *mmap_name, pid_t pid, struct nsinfo *nsi, bool *in_pidns)
  {
-	char *p;
+	const char *p;
 	char *end = NULL;
 	pid_t pid2;
 
-- 
2.53.0

